;; -*- mode: fundamental; coding: utf-8 -*-
;; Second dbskkd-cdb test dictionary: three keys that also exist in
;; SKK-JISYO.test but with deliberately different values. It is used to prove
;; that the dictionary named by argv[1] wins over DBSKKD_JISYO
;; (case argv_overrides_env_var) and that the environment variable alone is
;; honoured (case dictionary_env_var).
;; okuri-nasi entries.
かんじ /幹事/
すずき /薄/
みず /瑞/
